@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@* Marketing shell for the public landing page (docs/plans/blazor-port-plan.md §4.7), replacing
   Pages/Shared/_LayoutLanding.cshtml for Landing specifically - _LayoutLanding itself stays
   (Login and the other Account pages still use it until they migrate later in the port; see
   ui-inventory.md "Layouts").

   Static SSR, no chrome, same as EmptyLayout: App.razor already supplies the single
   <!DOCTYPE html>/<head>/<body> shell (fonts, app.css, pre-paint theme script) for the whole
   app, so there is nothing left for this layout to own beyond wrapping the page body - unlike
   _LayoutLanding.cshtml, which had to provide its own <head> because Razor Pages has no
   equivalent shared root document. Per plan §4.7, this layout does not inject a theme itself
   (that happens once, for every page, in App.razor) - the eventual MainLayout is the one that
   will add real chrome around @@Body. *@
@Body
